---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'

const starship = `[character]
success_symbol = "[❯](bold foam)"
error_symbol = "[❯](bold love)"
vimcmd_symbol = "[❮](bold iris)"

[directory]
truncation_length = 3
truncate_to_repo = true
truncation_symbol = "…/"`

const nv = `# pipe any command's output into a Neovim scratch buffer
alias -g NV='| nvim -'

rg TODO NV
git diff NV`

const eza = `alias ls='eza --group-directories-first --icons'
alias ll='eza -l --group-directories-first --icons'
alias lt='eza --tree --group-directories-first --icons'`

const plugins = [
  ['lazy.nvim', 'manages all of the plugins'],
  ['telescope.nvim', 'finding files and searching across a project'],
  ['oil.nvim', 'editing the filesystem like a regular buffer'],
  ['nvim-treesitter', 'syntax highlighting'],
  ['nvim-lspconfig and mason', 'language servers and the tools they need'],
  ['blink.cmp and LuaSnip', 'completion and snippets'],
  ['conform.nvim and nvim-lint', 'formatting and linting'],
  ['gitsigns.nvim', 'git changes in the gutter'],
  ['which-key.nvim', 'a reminder of what each keymap does'],
  ['mini.nvim', 'a handful of small editing helpers'],
  ['obsidian.nvim and render-markdown.nvim', 'notes and Markdown'],
]
const cli = [
  ['bat', 'a cat replacement with syntax highlighting, which I also use for man pages'],
  ['delta', 'the pager for git diffs'],
  ['eza', 'a replacement for ls'],
  ['fd', 'a friendlier find'],
  ['fzf', 'fuzzy finding'],
  ['zoxide', 'jumping to directories I have been in before'],
  ['atuin', 'searching my shell history'],
  ['zsh-autosuggestions and fast-syntax-highlighting', 'suggestions and coloring as I type'],
]
---
<Base title="Uses" description="The editor, terminal, and command line tools Patrick Beal uses.">
  <header class="pb-6 pt-14">
    <p class="label mb-3">uses</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What I use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] text-muted-foreground">
      This is the setup I work in every day. I've included a few pieces of my config that you're welcome to copy, and
      I'll keep adding to this page as things change.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-site border-t border-border pt-8">
    <h2 id="editor">Editor</h2>
    <p>
      I use Neovim. My config is split into an <code>init.lua</code>, a <code>config</code> folder for options and
      keymaps, and a <code>plugins</code> folder with one file for each group of plugins.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {plugins.map(([name, what]) => <li><code>{name}</code> for {what}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      A few keymaps I use all the time are <code>&lt;leader&gt;sf</code> to find files, <code>&lt;leader&gt;sg</code> to
      search with live grep, and <code>-</code> to open the parent directory in oil.
    </p>
    <p>I also use Claude Code for most of my development.</p>

    <h2 id="terminal">Terminal</h2>
    <p>
      On my Mac I use Otty with zsh and tmux. When I have to work on Windows, I use WezTerm with WSL. Everything is themed
      with Rosé Pine so that the terminal, tmux, and Neovim all match.
    </p>
    <p>
      My prompt is Starship. It shows the directory, the git branch and status, the language version, and how long the
      last command took if it was more than a couple of seconds. The prompt character turns red when the last command
      failed, which makes it a lot easier to find my place when the output gets long.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{starship}</code></pre>

    <h2 id="cli">Command line tools</h2>
    <ul>
      {cli.map(([name, what]) => <li><code>{name}</code> for {what}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      One small thing I use a lot is a global alias that sends the output of any command into Neovim, so I can search
      and scroll through it there.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{nv}</code></pre>
    <p>These are my aliases for <code>eza</code>.</p>
    <pre><code>{eza}</code></pre>
  </div>
</Base>
